Scope: drives the core's Idle screen selection to Screensaver and grades whether the picture actually animates, using bright-centroid travel rather than frame difference. It proves the OSD word reaches misterplexd and that the screensaver renderer moves; it does NOT prove the OSD menu navigation works from a real keyboard, does not check the animation's appearance, does not fix the separate per-scanline presentation damage, and restores the OSD selection it changed.
CONF OSD_CONTROL=1
DAEMON_LOG_AFTER_SELECTION:
  (nothing — the daemon did not react to the OSD word)
